{% comment %}
  sections/home-footer.liquid
  Ported from the "Arcane Flame Website Prototype" option-c.html:
    - CSS: lines ~361-372 (.foot, .foot__grid, .foot__brand img,
      .foot__brand p, .foot h5, .foot ul, .foot ul a, .foot ul a:hover,
      .foot__base) plus the .foot__grid-relevant slice of the <=1080px
      and <=680px responsive rules — see
      shopify-theme/assets/home-footer.css for the full colour-
      substitution notes.
    - Markup: the <footer class="foot">...</footer> block (brand blurb,
      three link columns — Print / Shop / Help — and the base bar with
      copyright + DM Stash attribution line).

  One-section-vs-two decision: built as its own section, separate from
  the final CTA banner (see home-final-cta.liquid) — see that file's
  header for the full reasoning. Short version: the footer is
  conventionally global/site-wide in Shopify themes (assigned once, in
  every template's JSON, or promoted to theme.liquid) while the CTA
  banner above it is homepage-specific content a merchant may want to
  reorder or drop independently. Splitting them lets a merchant do that
  without touching the other.

  Each footer column (Print / Shop / Help) is its own `link_list`
  setting, following the exact pattern home-nav.liquid already
  established for its single `menu` setting — just three of them here,
  each with its own editable heading text setting defaulting to the
  source's column titles. This means NO footer link/URL is hardcoded in
  this file: every link a merchant sees comes from whatever Shopify menu
  they assign to each of the three settings in the theme editor, which is
  also how the "footer links must resolve to real Shopify pages, not #"
  requirement gets satisfied in practice — it's on the merchant to build
  real menus (ideally pointing Help-column items at real policy pages via
  Shopify's Online Store > Navigation, and Print/Shop items at the
  calculator page / collections once they exist) rather than on this
  section to guess URLs that don't exist yet. See the task report for the
  full audit of which of the source's *default* link targets are real
  Shopify routes today vs. still-needed pages/collections.

  Logo judgment call: kept the home-nav.liquid / home-hero.liquid
  precedent — reference `arcane-flame-white.png` via `asset_url` rather
  than an `image_picker` setting. The brief notes an `image_picker` would
  actually be more correct for a real Shopify footer (letting a merchant
  swap their logo without a deploy), and that's true in isolation — but
  the header and footer logo should always be the *same* file, and
  splitting it into two independently-editable settings (one per section)
  creates a real risk a merchant updates one and not the other, producing
  a header/footer logo mismatch. Kept the single asset-file precedent
  instead, consistent with the known tracked gap (the file doesn't exist
  in shopify-theme/assets/ yet) already flagged for home-nav.liquid and
  home-hero.liquid.

  The DM Stash attribution line is an editable `text` setting (not
  hardcoded) per the brief — unlike the wording-constrained
  AttributionLockup badge in home-services.liquid, which had a specific
  tamper-proof requirement, footer copy here is ordinary editable content
  and the default text is simply the legally-reviewed exact wording.
{% endcomment %}
<footer class="foot">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="foot__grid">
      <div class="foot__brand">
        <img src="{{ 'arcane-flame-white.png' | asset_url }}" alt="{{ shop.name }}" />
        <div>{{ section.settings.brand_blurb }}</div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h5>{{ section.settings.print_heading }}</h5>
        <ul>
          {% for link in section.settings.print_links.links %}
            <li><a href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.title }}</a></li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h5>{{ section.settings.shop_heading }}</h5>
        <ul>
          {% for link in section.settings.shop_links.links %}
            <li><a href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.title }}</a></li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h5>{{ section.settings.help_heading }}</h5>
        <ul>
          {% for link in section.settings.help_links.links %}
            <li><a href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.title }}</a></li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="foot__base">
      <span>{{ section.settings.copyright_text }}</span>
      <span>{{ section.settings.attribution_text }}</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>

{{ 'brand-tokens.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'home-base.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'home-footer.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Footer",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "brand_blurb",
      "label": "Brand blurb",
      "default": "<p>High-detail resin and PLA 3D printing for tabletop gamers, makers and painters. Printed to order in the UK.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Print column"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "print_heading",
      "label": "Column heading",
      "default": "Print"
    },
    {
      "type": "link_list",
      "id": "print_links",
      "label": "Print column menu"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Shop column"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "shop_heading",
      "label": "Column heading",
      "default": "Shop"
    },
    {
      "type": "link_list",
      "id": "shop_links",
      "label": "Shop column menu"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Help column"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "help_heading",
      "label": "Column heading",
      "default": "Help"
    },
    {
      "type": "link_list",
      "id": "help_links",
      "label": "Help column menu"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Base bar"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "copyright_text",
      "label": "Copyright line",
      "default": "© 2026 Arcane Flame. All rights reserved."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "attribution_text",
      "label": "Attribution line",
      "info": "Legally-reviewed licensing-relationship wording — edit with care.",
      "default": "Officially licensed printer for DM Stash. Not affiliated with DM Stash."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Footer"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
